  "problem": "The disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}$ of events ${A}_{1},{A}_{2},{A}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space. Compute $P({A}_{1}|B)$ given the following probabilities:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P(B|{A}_{1})=0, & P({A}_{1})=0.25 \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{2})=0.6, & P({A}_{2})=0.25 \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{3})=0.3, & P({A}_{3})=0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
